1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Today we are going to test how subtitles behave during a normal spoken video.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The first thing we want to verify is whether every sentence appears at exactly the correct moment.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
The text should remain clearly visible without moving unexpectedly between different frames.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Short sentences should not become excessively large compared with the rest of the subtitles.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Longer sentences should wrap naturally across multiple lines without touching the edges of the video.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The distance between the subtitle and the bottom of the screen should remain completely consistent.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Every line should preserve the same alignment even when the amount of text changes considerably.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
We also want to make sure punctuation does not create unusual spacing between individual words.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The subtitle renderer should produce exactly the same result when the same frame is rendered repeatedly.

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Changing from one subtitle to the next should happen cleanly without showing both sentences together.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
There should never be a frame where an old subtitle remains visible because of an incorrect cache entry.

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The final sentence should disappear exactly when its assigned time range reaches the end.
